        <mxCell id="title" value="Aroma Pacífico — Identity Kinds, Directories, MFA Policies, Scopes and Encryption Keys" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=28;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="25" width="3760" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="Point 2 Security &amp; Identity Architecture (docs/security-and-identity.md, docs/landing-zone.md §4 | ASM-090..ASM-099, ADR-001, ADR-002, ADR-003, B06 [D06])" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=14.5;fontColor=#334155;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="68" width="3760" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_left_container" value="1. KINDS OF IDENTITY, DIRECTORIES &amp; ENTRY POINTS (Sections 2, 3, 5, 6)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#334155;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="40" y="115" width="1860" height="1530" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_workforce" value="KIND 1: WORKFORCE — HUMANS WHO OPERATE AWS (Landing Zone §4, Security §5.3)&#10;• Directory: IAM Identity Center (Organization instance in Management Account, Delegated Admin in Security Account) [D06]&#10;• Authentication: Mandatory MFA via TOTP software token on EVERY sign-in. Zero IAM users, zero static access keys (A08 §3.1).&#10;• Permission Sets &amp; Session Lifetimes (Narrow operations sets exempt from production-change SCP | A08 §3.1):&#10;  - PlatformReadOnly: Workload &amp; Network accounts. Read-only on resources, CloudWatch metrics, AWSIotLogsV2, audit logs. (4 hours)&#10;  - DeviceRevocation: Workload accounts. iot:UpdateCertificate, DetachPolicy, DetachThingPrincipal, UpdateThing fallback. (1 hour)&#10;  - IdentitySupport: Workload accounts. cognito-idp:AdminDisableUser, AdminUserGlobalSignOut, AdminAdd/RemoveUserFromGroup. (1 hour)&#10;  - Auditor: Security account. Read audit archive through Amazon Athena queries and organization CloudTrail (ASM-099). (4 hours)&#10;  - BreakGlass: All accounts. Emergency administrator access; every use immediately alerts platform operators and auditor. (1 hour)&#10;• Pipeline Boundary: Platform operators change production infrastructure ONLY through GitHub OIDC pipeline, never via permission sets." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="160" width="890" height="400" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="icon_sso" value="Identity Center" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.single_sign_on;fillColor=#DD344C;strokeColor=#ffffff;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="870" y="175" width="48" height="48" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_d06_sso" value="D06" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="905" y="165" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_pipeline_services" value="KIND 4: CI/CD PIPELINES &amp; PLATFORM SERVICE IDENTITIES (ADR-003, Security §2, B06)&#10;• CI/CD Pipeline Identity:&#10;  - Provider: GitHub Actions via GitHub OIDC Identity Provider in each environment account (dev, qa, pdn) [D06, D11, D12].&#10;  - Authentication: OIDC token exchanged for short-lived AWS STS assume-role credentials (ADR-003). Zero static keys in repo or state.&#10;  - Scoped Roles: Separate Plan Role (read-only state + dry run) and Apply Role (least privilege per domain stack) (ASM-051).&#10;• Platform IAM Service Roles (Least Privilege, Security Stack B06 [D06]):&#10;  - Inference Function Roles: 4 Bedrock vision function roles; granted bedrock:InvokeModel; DENIED personal and restricted keys.&#10;  - Threshold Function Role [D10]: Consumes SQS threshold queue; evaluates reading; writes alerts; calls SNS alert dispatcher.&#10;  - Reception Function Role: Links S3 flight objects to mission records; quarantines unauthorized objects; DENIED personal key.&#10;  - IoT Core Topic Rule Role [D09]: Assumed by IoT rules engine to write DynamoDB telemetry table and publish to SQS threshold queue.&#10;  - Sack Lookup Service Role: Lambda Function URL role; granted DynamoDB GetItem on buyer_view ONLY; ZERO access to records/personal." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="970" y="160" width="910" height="400" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="icon_iam_roles" value="IAM Roles" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.sts;fillColor=#DD344C;strokeColor=#ffffff;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1810" y="175" width="48" height="48" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_d06_iam" value="D06" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1845" y="165" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_app_users_header" value="KIND 2: APPLICATION USERS — AMAZON COGNITO DIRECTORY ARCHITECTURE (Security §3, §4.1, §5 | ASM-090)&#10;• Managed Directory: Amazon Cognito user pools on Essentials feature plan in us-east-1, Workload Account (pdn, qa, dev) [D06].&#10;• Two Separate User Pools: Pool-wide MFA setting enforces security boundaries by infrastructure configuration, not application logic.&#10;• Token Architecture: JWT tokens (ID, Access, Refresh). Token carries sub, phone/email, and group. NO scopes or farm lists inside tokens!&#10;• Pre-Authentication Trigger: Lambda trigger strictly enforces 1 identity = 1 role; rejects sign-in if user has multiple groups (ASM-099)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="580" width="1820" height="100" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="icon_cognito_main" value="Cognito" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.cognito;fillColor=#DD344C;strokeColor=#ffffff;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1810" y="595" width="48" height="48" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_d06_cog" value="D06" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1845" y="585" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_pool_staff" value="STAFF USER POOL: staff (MFA REQUIRED | TOTP | §3.2, §5.1)&#10;• MFA Policy: REQUIRED software token TOTP from authenticator app.&#10;• Sign-In: Username + Password + TOTP code. Token revocation enabled.&#10;• Sensitive Staff Step-Up Authentication (ASM-092):&#10;  - Operations: Fumigation authorization, threshold update, revocation, identity admin.&#10;  - Rule: Token auth_time must be &lt;= 10 minutes old; otherwise app prompts for fresh TOTP.&#10;• Groups &amp; Client Applications:&#10;  - collection_center_operator: Logistics workstation app &amp; reports web. (Own center)&#10;  - drone_operator: Drone ground-station app (10.4x.2.10). (Assigned missions)&#10;  - agronomist: Reports web. Authorizes fumigations (ADR-002). (Department scope)&#10;  - platform_operator: Reports web operations screens. (Whole platform, no business writes)&#10;• Token Lifetimes: Access token 60 min, Refresh token 30 days (ASM-092)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f3ff;strokeColor=#7c3aed;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#4c1d95;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="80" y="695" width="860" height="305" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_mfa_req" value="MFA: TOTP" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#7c3aed;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="830" y="705" width="90" height="90" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_pool_field" value="FIELD USER POOL: field (NO MFA, JUSTIFIED ADOPTION DECISION | §3.2, §5.2 | ASM-091)&#10;• MFA Policy: OFF. Intentional design decision based on case statement constraints:&#10;  - Adoption: Farmers distrust leaving notebook; farmer app has few simple screens.&#10;  - Connectivity: Operates in rural areas without continuous data coverage; offline outbox.&#10;  - Blast Radius: Narrow scope (own farms / own trips); compromised token cannot touch others.&#10;• Sign-In: Passwordless one-time code (SMS to registered phone for farmers/transporters; Email for buyers).&#10;• Compensating Security Controls:&#10;  - Hardware Keystore: App outbox encrypted with key in phone hardware keystore (ASM-095).&#10;  - Installation Binding: Every transaction carries unique mobile installation device_id (A10 §7).&#10;  - Local Phone Lock: App opens only after phone biometric or screen lock PIN challenge.&#10;  - Scope Enforcement: Server-side API validates caller owns target farm or trip on every call.&#10;• Groups: farmer (Own farms), transporter (Own trips), buyer (Read-only buyer view)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0f9ff;strokeColor=#0284c7;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0c4a6e;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="960" y="695" width="900" height="305" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_mfa_off" value="NO MFA (ASM-091)" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1730" y="705" width="120" height="120" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_devices" value="KIND 3: FIELD DEVICES — AWS IOT CORE REGISTRY &amp; AUTHENTICATION (Security §6, ADR-003, Connectivity §4)&#10;• Hardware Identity Directory: AWS IoT Core Thing Registry in workload account (pdn, qa, dev) [D08, D09].&#10;• Mutual TLS Authentication: Every device authenticates with a unique X.509 client certificate registered from a CSR generated on-device (ADR-003, ASM-010).&#10;  - Private key never leaves device hardware non-volatile secure storage; never seen by Terraform, pipeline, or human operator.&#10;  - Port 8883 (MQTT over TLS) or Port 443 with ALPN (protocol iot-mqtt). TLS 1.2+ security policy (IoTSecurityPolicy_TLS13_1_2_2022_10 | PD-100).&#10;• Dynamic IoT Policy Variables (One policy serves 200 or 1,000 farms without naming individual devices | ADR-003):&#10;  - iot:Connect allowed ONLY if client ID equals ${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName} and ${iot:Connection.Thing.IsAttached} is true.&#10;  - Farm Nodes (Crop &amp; Drying, 2 per farm | ASM-070): Publish ONLY to telemetry/${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}. Subscribe DENIED.&#10;  - 24-Hour Offline Buffer: Stores readings locally during signal outages; drains oldest-first upon reconnection (ASM-074).&#10;• Drone Kit Identity &amp; Upload Grant Binding Protocol (ADR-002, Security §6, ASM-093, PD-075 closed):&#10;  - Drone Kit: Paired flight vehicle and ground station (ASM-093). Subscribes ONLY to drones/${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}/grants.&#10;  - Pilot-to-Drone Binding:&#10;    1. Pilot signs into staff Cognito pool with MFA; requests upload grant for specific mission from API Gateway.&#10;    2. API validates: pilot assigned to order, pilot Aerocivil permit active (ASM-020), kit assigned, kit certificate ACTIVE in IoT registry.&#10;    3. API creates upload grant in DB and publishes 15-minute S3 pre-signed URLs on kit grant topic.&#10;    4. Ground station uploads imagery/flight records to S3; reception Lambda accepts object ONLY if grant pilot and kit were active at upload." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="1020" width="1820" height="310" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="icon_iot" value="IoT Core" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.iot_core;fillColor=#7AA116;strokeColor=#ffffff;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1810" y="1035" width="48" height="48" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_d08_dev" value="D08" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1845" y="1025" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_entry_points" value="APPLICATION ENTRY POINTS &amp; NETWORK BOUNDARIES (Connectivity §3, §9, Addressing §4 [D04], Sack &amp; Trip §7.2 [PD-051])&#10;• Anonymous Public Sack Lookup Front Door: Amazon CloudFront CDN + AWS WAF (rate limited &lt;= 30 req/min per IP | PD-102) -&gt; Lambda Function URL via OAC.&#10;  - Empty public_query tier; zero load balancer, zero NAT gateway charges (PD-051 closed). Reads ONLY buyer_view DynamoDB projection.&#10;• Application API Front Door: Amazon API Gateway custom domain (HTTPS, TLS 1.2 policy) -&gt; Regional public endpoint for mobile apps;&#10;  - Private VPC execute-api interface endpoint in application tier (10.82.48.0/20) for Collection Center logistics posts via IPsec TGW VPN [D04, D05].&#10;• S3 Interface Endpoint: Located in object_storage tier (10.82.80.0/20) reachable from collection center Soporte LAN (10.4x.2.10) for drone uploads.&#10;• Cognito Interface Endpoint: Located in application tier (10.82.48.0/20) allowing logistics staff to authenticate during WAN degradation." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ecfdf5;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#064e3b;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="1345" width="1820" height="180" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="icon_cf" value="CloudFront" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.cloudfront;fillColor=#8C4FFF;strokeColor=#ffffff;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1750" y="1355" width="42" height="42" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="icon_apigw" value="API Gateway" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.api_gateway;fillColor=#8C4FFF;strokeColor=#ffffff;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1810" y="1355" width="42" height="42" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_d04_ep" value="D04" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1845" y="1345" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_right_container" value="2. ROLES, LEAST PRIVILEGE, SCOPE ENFORCEMENT &amp; SEPARATION OF DUTIES (Sections 3.3, 4, 8, 9)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#334155;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1930" y="115" width="1870" height="1530" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_scopes" value="DYNAMIC SCOPE ENFORCEMENT MODEL (Security §3.3)&#10;• Scope Lives in Transactional Data, NOT in JWT Tokens:&#10;  - Tokens prove identity (sub) and role group (agronomist, farmer, etc.).&#10;  - Scopes are NOT encoded in tokens (avoids stale token revocation delays).&#10;  - Scope assignments are maintained as dynamic database records:&#10;    * Own farms: Farm-to-farmer membership (maintained by Platform Operator).&#10;    * Own trips: Trip-to-transporter record (created upon custody acceptance).&#10;    * Own center: Center operator to Cauca (10.41), Huila (10.42), Tolima (10.43).&#10;    * Assigned missions: Fumigation/survey order to pilot &amp; kit (Agronomist sets).&#10;    * Department: Agronomist to one or more departments (ASM-021).&#10;• Immediate Effect: Adding or removing an assignment takes effect on the NEXT API request.&#10;• Revocation Timestamp Check: API compares token auth_time against user&#x27;s revoked_after attribute.&#10;  Any token issued prior to revocation is rejected instantaneously without waiting for token expiry." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1950" y="160" width="890" height="360" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_invariants" value="SEPARATION OF DUTIES &amp; ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS (§4.3, ADR-002)&#10;• Invariant 1: Fumigation Authorization (ADR-002, Case Part E)&#10;  - Human Identity Only: Must be signed by agronomist staff token with fresh MFA.&#10;  - Zero Automated Trigger: No Lambda function, topic rule, or AI model authorizes.&#10;  - Separation: Authorizing agronomist CANNOT be the assigned pilot (authorizer_id != operator_id).&#10;• Invariant 2: Drone Operator Boundary&#10;  - Pilot executes missions, uploads imagery. CANNOT create, modify, or authorize orders.&#10;• Invariant 3: Platform Operator Boundary&#10;  - Manages tenant enrollment, user accounts, and infrastructure monitoring.&#10;  - CANNOT authorize fumigation; CANNOT write sacks, custody events, trips, or orders.&#10;• Invariant 4: One Identity = One Role (ASM-099)&#10;  - Pre-auth Lambda trigger strictly denies sign-in to users belonging to multiple role groups.&#10;• Invariant 5: Sensitive Staff Step-Up Authentication (ASM-092)&#10;  - Token auth_time must be &lt;= 10 min for fumigation auth, threshold change, or revocation." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#d97706;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#78350f;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="2860" y="160" width="920" height="360" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_role_matrix" value="ROLE-TO-DATA ACCESS MATRIX (Summary of Security §4.2 | Least Privilege by Role &amp; Scope)&#10;• Farmer (field | Own farms): Read farm records, node registry, crop/drying telemetry, alerts, soil analysis, threshold ranges, expected sacks, pest case status, fumigation window. Create/Read sack registrations. Create/Read own personal profile.&#10;• Transporter (field | Own trips): Read pickup points, sack code &amp; weight. Create/Read sack custody events (full trace) and port delivery. Create/Read own trip GPS positions. Read/Update own personal profile. Zero access to farmer cédula, telemetry, or other trips.&#10;• Collection-Center Operator (staff | Own center): Read farm name &amp; municipality delivering to center. Read/Create sack registrations &amp; local code bindings. Create reception accepted/rejected &amp; departure events. Read open trips to/from own center. Read expected harvest sacks. Read display name &amp; plate of delivering transporters. Zero access to farmer cédula or telemetry.&#10;• Read-Only Buyer &amp; Public Reader (field / anonymous): Read sack by code ONLY. Returns strictly the Buyer View Projection (origin, dates, status, drying variables). Zero access to farm records, farmer cédula, node IDs, custody events, trips, positions, weights.&#10;• Drone Operator (staff | Assigned missions): Read farm polygons &amp; no-fly zones for assigned missions. Read assigned mission package &amp; fumigation order. Create flight records &amp; drone object uploads via upload grants. Read/Update own personal profile. Zero create/auth permissions.&#10;• Agronomist (staff | Department): Read farm polygons; Create/Update plots &amp; preliminary no-fly zones (ASM-027). Read node registry, crop telemetry, alerts, harvest estimates, pest cases. Create/Read soil analyses. Authorize/Reject fumigation orders. Zero flight permissions.&#10;• Platform Operator (staff | Platform scope): Create/Update farm records at enrollment; revoke devices; update thresholds (step-up MFA | ASM-099); manage application identities, groups, and scopes. Read operational metadata &amp; audit logs. ZERO business data writes." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1950" y="535" width="1830" height="240" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_buyer_view" value="SACK CODE SECURITY &amp; THE PUBLIC BUYER VIEW PROJECTION (Security §8, Sack &amp; Trip §7, §10 | ASM-094, ASM-096, ASM-154)&#10;• Opaque Sack Identifier (ASM-094):&#10;  - Entropy: 80 cryptographically secure random bits generated on platform only (Crockford Base32: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-C with check symbol).&#10;  - Privacy Invariant: NEVER derived from cédula, name, farm ID, node ID, timestamp, sequential counter, or any hash thereof.&#10;  - Internal Decoupling: System keys sacks by internal UUID sack_id; sack code is a unique secondary index (damaged labels replaced without loss of history).&#10;• Architectural Enforcement via Dedicated Projection Store (buyer_view DynamoDB table | CMK public_view [D06]):&#10;  - Separation: Lookup service reads ONLY from the buyer_view projection table; holds ZERO IAM or KMS permissions on records, personal, or telemetry stores!&#10;  - 4 Authorized Data Groups (Case statement Point 2 mandate):&#10;    1. Origin: sack_code, department, municipality (coarse administrative boundary; no farm name, vereda, or coordinates).&#10;    2. Processing Dates: drying_start_date, drying_end_date, packing_date (calendar dates only; no timestamps of day).&#10;    3. Status: Current sack state (in preparation, en route to center, accepted/rejected at center, en route to port, delivered at port accepted/rejected).&#10;    4. Drying Variables: final_coffee_moisture_pct, grain_temperature_min_c, grain_temperature_mean_c, grain_temperature_max_c (drying lot summary).&#10;  - Explicitly Withheld: Farmer name, cédula, phone, subject_id, coordinates, node IDs, raw telemetry, transporter name/plate, custody times, weights, pest records." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f3ff;strokeColor=#7c3aed;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#4c1d95;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1950" y="790" width="1830" height="255" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_personal_retention" value="PERSONAL DATA LIFECYCLE, PRIVACY &amp; RETENTION ARCHITECTURE (Security §9 | ASM-098, ADR-001)&#10;• Personal Data Inventory &amp; Storage:&#10;  - Personal Data Table (DynamoDB | CMK personal [D06]): Stores farmer &amp; transporter full name, cédula, phone number, vehicle plate.&#10;  - Pseudonymous subject_id: All business transactions (sacks, trips, orders, flight logs) reference persons ONLY via random opaque subject_id.&#10;  - Cédula Protection: Nobody reads another person&#x27;s cédula except Platform Operator during support/enrollment. Logs carry subject_id or sub, never cédula.&#10;• 5-Year Retention Clock &amp; Anonymization Engine (ASM-098, Case Point 2):&#10;  - Retention Clock: Personal profile retained 5 years from user deactivation; transaction records retained 5 years from event timestamp.&#10;  - Monthly Anonymization Process: Amazon EventBridge Scheduler triggers Lambda function with scoped delete role:&#10;    * Deletes personal profile item (name, cédula, phone, plate) from personal_data table.&#10;    * Calls cognito-idp:AdminDeleteUser to permanently delete Cognito identity.&#10;    * Result: Transaction records preserve subject_id for traceability, permanently linked to nobody (full anonymization).&#10;  - DynamoDB Time-To-Live (TTL): expires_at attribute on event records and transporter positions triggers automatic serverless deletion at 5 years.&#10;  - S3 Object Expiration: S3 lifecycle rules automatically delete drone imagery and sack history JSON Lines exports after 5 years.&#10;  - Restricted Drone Imagery: Drone objects with a person (restricted/person/) encrypted under restricted key, excluded from inference, deleted after 5 years (ASM-165)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0f9ff;strokeColor=#0284c7;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0c4a6e;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1950" y="1060" width="1830" height="280" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_revocation_summary" value="REVOCATION POLICIES &amp; TIME LIMITS SUMMARY (Security §10 | Target SLA: Complete within 4 hours of report | ASM-098)&#10;• Decommissioned Farm Node / Stolen Node: Platform Operator executes iot:UpdateCertificate(REVOKED), DetachPolicy, DetachThingPrincipal, UpdateThing(status=decommissioned).&#10;  - Immediate Effect: IoT Core forcefully terminates active TLS sessions within minutes; detached policy denies all publish attempts; node buffer expires after 24h (ASM-074).&#10;• Lost Drone Kit: Same 4 IoT Core actions (status=lost). Mission upload grants refused; pre-signed S3 URLs expire in 15 min; incoming uploads quarantined in S3.&#10;• Departing Pilot / Agronomist: cognito-idp:AdminDisableUser, AdminUserGlobalSignOut, AdminRemoveUserFromGroup; DB sets revoked_after=NOW(). API denies calls immediately (0 min).&#10;• Lost Phone (Farmer / Transporter): AdminUserGlobalSignOut, marks installation device_id as revoked in DB, AdminDisableUser. Outbox rejected. Re-enrolls in person at center." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#dc2626;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#7f1d1d;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1950" y="1355" width="1830" height="170" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_bottom_container" value="3. ENCRYPTION AT REST (AWS KMS CUSTOMER-MANAGED KEYS) &amp; ENCRYPTION IN TRANSIT (Section 7)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#334155;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="40" y="1665" width="3760" height="795" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_kms_header" value="AWS KMS CUSTOMER-MANAGED KEYS (CMK) ARCHITECTURE — 8 KEYS PER ENVIRONMENT (Security §7.2, §7.3 | ADR-003, B06 [D06])&#10;Every store uses a dedicated customer-managed key of its data class, ensuring service roles receive cryptographic access ONLY to the data they require.&#10;Automatic Key Rotation: Enabled on ALL customer-managed keys with a 365-day rotation period (ASM-097). Previous key material preserved; zero re-encryption required.&#10;Deletion Protection: kms:ScheduleKeyDeletion and kms:DisableKey DENIED to all principals except BreakGlass; mandatory 30-day waiting period alerts operators." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="1710" width="2300" height="95" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="icon_kms_main" value="KMS CMK" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.key_management_service;fillColor=#DD344C;strokeColor=#ffffff;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="2280" y="1720" width="48" height="48" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="badge_d06_kms" value="D06" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0284c7;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11.5;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="2315" y="1710" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_2" value="KEY: telemetry [D06, D09] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: DynamoDB telemetry table (crop &amp; drying readings, 5-yr TTL) and transport_positions store.&#10;• Authorized Grantees: IoT topic rule role, telemetry Lambdas, reporting roles. DENIED to API general roles." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0f9ff;strokeColor=#0284c7;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="1815" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_3" value="KEY: objects [D06] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: Amazon S3 Drone Object Bucket (photos, orthomosaics, flight records, sack history export).&#10;• Authorized Grantees: Reception Lambda, Bedrock inference Lambdas, export Lambda. API pre-signing role (GenerateDataKey)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#16a34a;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="1893" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_4" value="KEY: records [D06] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: DynamoDB Transactional Tables (sacks, sack_event_log, trips, cases, orders, thresholds, upload grants).&#10;• Authorized Grantees: Application API Lambda execution roles, threshold function role. DENIED to public lookup." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#d97706;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="1971" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_5" value="KEY: personal [D06] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: DynamoDB personal_data table (farmer &amp; transporter cédula, name, phone, plate under subject_id).&#10;• Authorized Grantees: Enrollment &amp; support administrative roles ONLY. STRICTLY DENIED to inference and public lookup." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#dc2626;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="2049" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_6" value="KEY: logs [D06] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: Amazon CloudWatch Log Groups (/aws/application/audit, Lambda logs, AWSIotLogsV2, VPC Flow Logs).&#10;• Authorized Grantees: CloudWatch Logs service principal. Read-only to PlatformReadOnly and IdentitySupport." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f3ff;strokeColor=#7c3aed;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="2127" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_7" value="KEY: state [D02, D06] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: Amazon S3 Terraform Remote State Buckets (aroma-pdn-tfstate, aroma-qa-tfstate, aroma-dev-tfstate).&#10;• Authorized Grantees: GitHub OIDC plan and apply roles ONLY. prevent_destroy enabled on state bucket (ADR-003)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f1f5f9;strokeColor=#475569;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="2205" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_8" value="KEY: public_view [D06] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: DynamoDB buyer_view projection table (origin, processing dates, status, drying variables).&#10;• Authorized Grantees: Sack lookup Lambda Function URL role and buyer view projection updater Lambda ONLY." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#faf5ff;strokeColor=#9333ea;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="2283" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="key_9" value="KEY: restricted [D06] (CMK | Rotation: 365d | us-east-1)&#10;• Stores Protected: Amazon S3 prefix restricted/person/ (drone photos containing human beings; ASM-164, ASM-165).&#10;• Authorized Grantees: ZERO function or human roles hold grants. Explicit bucket-policy Deny; incident audit access only." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff1f2;strokeColor=#e11d48;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="60" y="2361" width="1140" height="72" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_cross_keys" value="CROSS-CUTTING KEYS (MANAGEMENT &amp; SECURITY ACCOUNTS | Landing Zone §7):&#10;• audit CMK (Security Account | D06):&#10;  - Encrypts Central S3 Audit Archive Bucket (s3://aroma-audit-archive-shared/).&#10;  - Enforces S3 Object Lock in compliance mode (5-year retention, ASM-067).&#10;  - Grantees: AWS CloudTrail (Multi-Region Trail), Amazon Data Firehose delivery, and Auditor Athena execution role.&#10;• budgets_sns CMK (Management Account | D06):&#10;  - Encrypts Amazon SNS budget alert notification topic. Grantees: AWS Budgets engine, AWS Cost Anomaly Detection." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f3ff;strokeColor=#7c3aed;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#4c1d95;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1220" y="1815" width="1140" height="150" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_key_gov" value="KEY ROTATION &amp; CRYPTOGRAPHIC DELETION GOVERNANCE (Security §7.3 | ASM-097):&#10;• 365-Day Automatic Rotation: KMS automatically rotates backing key material yearly.&#10;  Data is never re-encrypted; KMS transparently decrypts historical ciphertexts using retired keys.&#10;• Cryptographic Erasure Guardrail:&#10;  - Key policy explicitly DENIES kms:ScheduleKeyDeletion and kms:DisableKey to all roles.&#10;  - BreakGlass role is the sole identity capable of scheduling key deletion under emergency audit.&#10;  - Maximum 30-day deletion waiting period enforced; alerts platform operators upon initiation.&#10;• Strict Principal Isolation: No wildcard principals allowed; cross-environment decryption strictly prohibited." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#d97706;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#78350f;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1220" y="1980" width="1140" height="150" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_edge_enc" value="EDGE BUFFER &amp; LOCAL STORAGE ENCRYPTION (Security §7.1 | Connectivity §4, §7 | ASM-095):&#10;• Farm Node Flash Storage: Non-volatile circular buffer encrypted locally; retains max 24 hours of readings (ASM-074).&#10;• Mobile Outboxes: Farmer &amp; transporter mobile apps encrypt local queue with keys stored in hardware-backed Android Keystore / iOS Secure Enclave (ASM-095).&#10;• Drone Ground Station: Contracted drone company required by agreement to encrypt all local flight storage and image caches (ASM-095)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ecfdf5;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#064e3b;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1220" y="2145" width="1140" height="110" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="c_transit_enc" value="ENCRYPTION IN TRANSIT — ZERO UNENCRYPTED FLOWS (Security §7.1, Connectivity §2)&#10;Every network flow utilizes TLS 1.2 or higher end-to-end; no proxy, relay, or load balancer terminates TLS (A10 §2).&#10;• AWS IoT Core Data Endpoint (Port 8883 / 443 ALPN):&#10;  - Mutual TLS (mTLS) with client certificates; security policy IoTSecurityPolicy_TLS13_1_2_2022_10 (PD-100).&#10;• Public Front Door (CloudFront &amp; Public Sack Lookup):&#10;  - HTTPS only. Enforces minimum protocol TLSv1.2_2021 with AWS WAF inspection (PD-051 closed).&#10;• Application API Gateway (Public &amp; Private Endpoints):&#10;  - Custom domain enforcing HTTPS only with security policy TLS_1_2. HTTP requests refused/redirected.&#10;• Amazon S3 Buckets (Drone Objects, Exports, Audit Archive):&#10;  - Bucket policies strictly DENY requests with aws:SecureTransport: false or s3:TlsVersion &lt; 1.2.&#10;  - Uploads carry SHA-256 per-part checksums validated on ingestion (A10 §6).&#10;• Collection Center WAN (Site-to-Site VPN):&#10;  - Dual IPsec IKEv2 tunnels connecting each center firewall to AWS Transit Gateway hub in network account (ASM-078).&#10;  - Center LAN traffic to cloud interface endpoints is itself encrypted TLS inside the IPsec tunnel.&#10;• Service-to-Service Communication (Within AWS):&#10;  - AWS SDK calls over HTTPS/TLS; VPC traffic reaches AWS services via AWS PrivateLink interface endpoints (execute-api, cognito-idp, S3, logs) without crossing public internet [D04, PC-IAC-020]." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0f9ff;strokeColor=#0284c7;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0c4a6e;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="2390" y="1710" width="1390" height="735" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
